From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mmis1000 <mmis10002@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:15:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] Terminal lifetime: persistent or window-owned terminals
 on the remote pty host

- Pty host tracks windows by heartbeat; a window-owned terminal ends a grace
  period after its owner window goes away, Reload Window keeps it.
- Persistent terminals ignore the reconnection grace timers and keep the
  server from auto-shutting down (PtyHostKeepAlive).
- Make Persistent / Make Window-owned commands and a tab status marker.
- A window forgets a pty when it detaches, so it stops answering the orphan
  question for terminals it no longer shows.
- Remote terminals are no longer revived from a saved buffer, which started
  duplicate shells next to the running ones.
